Concurrent Update

A Concurrent Update Error occurs when two Spark jobs try to update the same Delta table (or the same data) at the same time.

Delta Lake uses Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC):

Both jobs read the same table version.
The first job commits successfully.
The second job checks the table before committing.
Since the table has already changed, Delta detects the conflict and rejects the second job with a concurrent update error.
Example
Job A: MERGE INTO customer
Job B: DELETE FROM customer
Both modify the same customer records simultaneously
How to resolve it
Schedule jobs so they don't overlap

