Z-Ordering is a Delta Lake optimization that physically rearranges data in files based on one or more frequently filtered columns, so related values are stored close together.

This improves data skipping, meaning Spark reads fewer files, resulting in faster query performance.
We typically apply it after OPTIMIZE on columns commonly used in filters or joins, such as customer_id or date."
